  "rewritten_answer": "There are three primary grammatical cases in Arabic: الرفع (raf'), النصب (nasb), and الجر (jarr). الرفع is used for the subject, the predicate, and the doer. النصب is used for the done-to (object) and after certain particles (حروف) that trigger it. الجر is used for a noun that comes after a preposition."
}"

